description=Quality-of-life tools for Project Zomboid. Highlights loose items on the ground, including items added by other mods.<LINE><LINE>
description=Controls: Click the flashlight beside the sidebar Inventory button; a checkmark means ON. The tools icon opens Wishlist, menu rules and settings. F8 is the default optional shortcut.<LINE>
description=Wishlist: Personal and shared item lists, inventory and crafting integration, and wanted-item ground highlights. Open with K; configure under Survivor Wishlist in Mod Options.<LINE><LINE>
description=Settings: Change the shortcut, colour, radius and enabled state in Options > Mods > PZ Survivor Toolkit.<LINE><LINE>
description=Visibility: Only items in your character's current field of view are highlighted. Previously explored tiles alone are not enough.<LINE>
description=Rendering: Uses native outlines or colour tints, depending on the item renderer.<LINE><LINE>
description=Clothing comparisons: Optional neutral grey for zero changes in the Wear menu. Gains and losses retain the game's configured colours.<LINE><LINE>
description=Multiplayer auto-drink: Respects each player's own setting, including changes in Options. The host's saved preference no longer blocks other players.<LINE><LINE>
description=Vehicle mechanics: Optional Uninstall to ground beside the native Uninstall action, for any removable part without a weight threshold. Native tools, skills, duration and success checks remain in effect. Requires Toolkit on the server and every client.<LINE><LINE>
description=Inventory presentation: Built-in container capacity bars, magazine segments and expanded Item Details share native/CleanUI layout. Load CleanUI before Toolkit; disable separate ContainerCapacityIndicator and BravoItemDetails mods. Existing preferences are preserved.<LINE><LINE>
description=Research and planting: Native research availability and known planting seasons are shown on inventory items. Growing details include water, growth time and month lists; previous Seed Season Indicator preferences are preserved. Disable separate HasResearch and SeedSeasonIndicator.<LINE><LINE>
description=Item Details: Shows uses, condition, sharpness, ammunition, food and Nutritionist values, fluids and clothing holes. Preserves complete stacks and selection while sorting the configured prefix, including organizedCategories vehicle parts. Configure Toolkit Item Details in Mod Options.<LINE><LINE>
description=TV & Radio ReInvented: Keeps windows open and adds a close button. Click loaded VHS to eject; select tapes from reachable containers or drag them onto the slot. Fully watched tapes have the inventory checkmark. Configurable in Mod Options. Fixes device recognition and native macOS video paths; the separate TVRadioReinventedFix4220 is no longer needed.<LINE><LINE>
description=Context menus: Groups known actions, removes exact duplicates and puts common actions above secondary/destructive commands using stable priorities for carried items, loot, world and vehicles. Batch operations appear once per selection while distinct targets and native single-item actions remain available.<LINE><LINE>
description=Quartermaster: Built-in storage designations, automatic distribution, storage Manifest and ingredient fetching for vanilla/Neat Crafting. Existing Quartermaster settings, assignments and presets are retained. Disable the separate Quartermaster Workshop mod.<LINE><LINE>
description=Item tags: Independent tags derived from organizedCategories, colored labels and native pictograms in native/CleanUI inventory, named all/any filters with exclusions and a match preview, and saved dynamic Quartermaster rules. Legacy category IDs remain unchanged for other mods. Can be disabled in Mod Options.<LINE><LINE>
description=Inventory: Optional Grab/Put amount with one whole-number budget across the selection; favourites and equipped items are skipped. Disabled with TakeAnyAmount active. Toolkit owns category filters when Better Containers is active. Select categories from the Category header dropdown. CleanUI searches hide nonmatching items. Fixes grouped-item arrow spacing. Inventory filters can be disabled in Mod Options. Preserves marquee and Shift selection across inventory redraws and combined proximity views.<LINE><LINE>
description=Batch clothing: Cut selected clothing from the native cut/rip submenu. Supports cotton, denim and leather with native tools and outputs; skips favourites and worn/held items. Can be disabled independently in Mod Options.<LINE><LINE>
description=Bulk dismantle: Select watches or other supported electronics and choose Dismantle selected from the native dismantling submenu. Processes only selected instances using native recipes, tools, time and XP. Skips favourites and worn/held items. Can be disabled in Mod Options.<LINE><LINE>
description=Medicine indicators: Eight independent MoodleFramework indicators, with authoritative multiplayer readings and optional black sage/common mallow effects. Lemongrass reads the native cooldown through matching Toolkit Java Patches. Separate switches appear only with MoodleFramework and without MedicineMoodlesB42.<LINE><LINE>
description=Navigator: Optional original textured monitor housing tinted to the dashboard, flush docking and adaptive map size for vanilla and all Realistic Dashboard driver styles. Keeps native routes, controls and dragging; disable in Mod Options to restore the original UI.<LINE><LINE>
description=Context menus: Automatically groups known actions across native inventory, world, vehicle and health menus. Short menus stay compact and unknown mod commands remain visible. Optional client-local editor supports group overrides, hiding and reset. Disable in Mod Options to restore the original menus. Hidden when Context Menu Organizer or its World variant is active.<LINE><LINE>
description=Compatibility: Build 42.19 or newer within Build 42. No additional mod dependencies. Auto-drink tested with two local multiplayer clients on B42.21. Split-screen has not been verified.<LINE><LINE>
description=Source: https://github.com/AlexRedby/pz-survivor-toolkit
versionMin=42.19
